terion":"F[P-](F)(F)(F)(F)F","record_id":"MLDB-000258","detection":"ICP-MS","method_description":"Lipophilicity was presented as the log Po/w values, which were determined using the flask-shaking method [37]. An aliquot of stock solution of the iridium complex or copolymer in an aqueous NaCl solution (0.9% w/v and saturated with octan-1-ol) was added to an equal volume of octan-1-ol (saturated with 0.9% w/v NaCl) and shaken for 2 h at 60 rpm to allow partition at 298 K. After the sample was centrifuged at 3000 rpm for 10 min, the aqueous layer was carefully separated from the octan-1-ol layer for iridium analysis. Iridium-193 in the aqueous phase (this concentration corresponded to [Ir]w) was determined by ICP-MS and the partition coefficient (Po/w) for each complex was calculated as the ratio [Ir]o/[Ir]w, where [Ir]o was obtained by subtraction of the iridium content of the aqueous layer after partition from the iridium content of the aqueous layer before partition."},{"abbreviation_in_the_article":"1c","value":1.91,"value_relation":"=","std":0.024,"type_authors":"logP","method":"shake-flask","aqueous_phase":"0.9% NaCl","doi":"10.1109/nanomed.2010.5749807","year":2010,"counterion":"F[P-](F)(F)(F)(F)F","record_id":"MLDB-001422","detection":"UV-Vis","method_description":"The lipophilicity of the complexes has been determined by shake-flask method (10.1007/s002800000166)."}]}